From 82de783a02303cf7cb2413ae5c67bc617fe3be71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:11:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 01/28] statusline: show Furiosa NPU model state with per-model
 LEDs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Furiosa router lazy-serves models onto four NPU cards; a tp32 model takes
all four and needs ~2 minutes to load. Until now the TUI said nothing during
that, and it could not show that several small models share the cards.

- services/npuStatus.ts polls the router's /router/status. Interval adapts:
  1s while any model is loading/stopping, 10s when idle. The first probe that
  fails disables polling for the session, so pointing openclaude at a non-Furiosa
  OpenAI endpoint costs exactly one request.
- BuiltinStatusLine renders one segment per model: green when up, yellow while
  loading/stopping, red when the selected model is not on a card yet. Terminals
  have no CSS animation, so transitioning models blink by alternating ●/○ on
  each poll tick — the poll *is* the animation clock.
- The selected model is marked ▶ and given a low priority so it survives a
  narrow terminal; the other cards' models yield first via the existing
  fitSegments degradation.
- When the NPU segments are present they replace the plain model-name segment,
  which would otherwise repeat the same name and waste width.

Verified against the live 4-card server: Qwen3-4B-FP8@dp2 observed through
loading → up, and this build answered a prompt through the router.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
