Subject: [PATCH 04/28] model picker: say why the NPU config row is absent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A model that occupies every card has exactly one parallel configuration, so the
row rendered nothing — indistinguishable from a broken feature. The default
model (gpt-oss-120b, tp32) is one of those, so opening /model showed no row at
all and looked like nothing had been implemented.

Render a dimmed explanation instead, mirroring the existing 'Effort not
supported' line. Only when the backend actually publishes @dp/@pp variants, so
non-NPU providers keep rendering nothing.

