From 9fac9610ac516823d08dd38a92918e9231766dd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:48:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 08/28] model picker: adjust dp and pp as separate axes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The row cycled through whole configurations — dp1·pp1, dp2·pp1, dp1·pp2,
dp2·pp2 — so reaching a particular pp meant walking past unrelated dp values.
People pick these separately.

Now each axis has its own row of values, ←/→ moves the active one and tab
switches between them (free in this context; shift+tab is already the global
permission-mode cycle).

The axes cannot be fully independent: dp x pp is bounded by the card count and
the backend only advertises servable combinations. Each axis therefore offers
only the values reachable while the other is held, and a move that would strand
the partner repairs it — from dp4·pp1, stepping pp lands on dp2·pp2 rather than
an id that does not exist. FXB artifacts, which cannot do pipeline parallelism
at all, simply show pp with a single value.

