Subject: [PATCH 11/28] model picker: start loading the model as soon as it is
 picked
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The router serves lazily, so picking a model did nothing until the first message
was sent — and a large model then takes a couple of minutes, with no sign that
anything had begun. Selecting now fires /router/preload, which returns
immediately and loads in the background, so the LED starts moving right away.

Fire-and-forget: a backend without the endpoint is unaffected, and the model
still loads on first use as before.

