From: hyunjun1234 <plab2090@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 13:47:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 15/28] model picker: support a per-model default pp (large
 models like bf16 coder)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Some builds are too big for one card (bf16 30B ≈ 57GB) so their smallest
servable config is pp2, not pp1. The router now reports a `pp_default` per
model in FURIO_NPU_META; mirror the tp mechanism:

- ppDefaultOf(base) from the meta; parseNpuVariant fills pp from it when the
  id has no @pp suffix; variantId omits @pp at the default. So the bare id
  round-trips to pp2 and the pp axis shows [2,3,4] (never the OOM pp1).
- Unchanged for normal models (pp_default defaults to 1).
- tests: bare→pp2, axis lists [2,3,4], @pp only off-default, no tp axis.
