From 0e8f078c651831ace7bdc82ef48f72dfeff3823a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunjun1234 <plab2090@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:11:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 21/28] npu: background calls must follow the /model switch,
 not the launch model
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

getSmallFastModel() returned process.env.OPENAI_MODEL for the openai provider —
the model the process *launched* with. After /model switches models mid-session,
every background call (session title, topic check, away summary) kept firing at
the old id.

Against a normal endpoint that is merely untidy. Against the Furiosa NPU router
the stale id is a different model on the cards, and a tp32 model owns all four of
them, so one session-title request evicted the model the user was waiting on,
served the title, and then reloaded it (~100s). The user's turn was cut off
mid-stream: the model had streamed "I'll help you modify base_carter_run.py …"
and the tool call that follows it never arrived. The turn read as "it just
narrates and does nothing".

Follow the session override (what /model set) when there is one. With no override
this is byte-for-byte the previous behaviour, and ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL still
wins for anyone who genuinely wants a separate small model.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Na71jMPNwVCJecN1VMjJbo
