+/**
+ * What Enter on the ↓ switcher does for the highlighted model.
+ *
+ * Enter means "put this model on the cards", not "change the setting". Those
+ * came apart when the router had nothing loaded: the model already marked ▶ is
+ * the session model, so an equality guard around the whole branch made Enter on
+ * it do nothing at all — the one case where the user most needs it to load.
+ *
+ * So the preload is unconditional and only the model *switch* is guarded, since
+ * re-selecting the model you already have would just churn settings and state.
