 spectrum
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two problems with the inherited gradient. It split evenly between the row and
the column, so within one row the first and last letters sat half a palette
apart and a word stopped reading as one shape. And the palette was orange —
close enough to Claude's own mark to be confusing for a lab build.

Paint per letter instead: one flat color per letter cell, walking a nine-stop
cyan→magenta spectrum across SOTA and FURIO so the two words share one sweep.
Letter widths differ (FURIO's I is 3 columns, the rest are 9), so the cell
widths are data next to the art rather than a column arithmetic guess.

paintLine stays as upstream wrote it — unused here, but left alone so it does
not drift. Upstream palettes are untouched and still reachable from /logo.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Awg9EDmFe6qrrwt2T4HiDJ
